
#TYPE
* ================================================================
*  constant values

          * Version number of SPLC API, must be increased after every
          * incompatible change
  SPLC_API_VERSION                        K60          * SPLC-Api-Version

          *
          * Maximal numbers and sizes for SKERN
  S_T_AX_NO                               K22          * maximum number of axes (must be equal MAXAXIS)

  S_S_AX_NO                               K6          * maximum number of spindles (for NCK only)

  S_AG_MAX                                K8          * maximum number of axes Groups

  S_BOARD_NO                              K5          * maximum number of controller boards

  S_DRIVE_NO                              K8          * maximum number of drives on board

  S_DRIVE_MAX                             K40          * maximum number of drives

  S_AXES_MAX                              K24          * maximum number of axes

  FIRST_SPINDLE                           K22          * offset for 1. spindle (for iTNC only)

  S_MAX_BRAKES_AXIS                       K5          * maximum number of brakes connected to one motor

          *
          * Maximum number of markers and maximum number of words that are transferred from PLC MC
          * to SPLC CC
  SPLC_TRANSFER_M_SIZE                    K2          * number of unsigned for marker transfer

  SPLC_TRANSFER_D_COUNT                   K32          * maximum number of dwords transferred

  SPLC_TRANSFER_M_COUNT                   K64          *
          * maximum number of markers transferred

          *
          * The SPLC program for the CC is transferred in blocks. The following constant defines
          * how many lines of data each of theses blocks contains
  SPLC_NO_OF_LINES_PER_BLOCK              K99          * Definition for axis group type

  S_AG_NO                                 K-1          * axis group is not used

  S_AG_NC                                 K0          * axis group type feed axes

  S_AG_SP                                 K1          * axis group type spindle

  S_AG_TCH                                K2          * axis group type tool axes

          *
          * Maximal sizes and numbers for SPLC
  SPLC_TIMER_COUNT                        K16          * number of SPLC timers

  SPLC_INV_I_LIMIT                        K8          * maximum number of inputs with inverse logic

  SPLC_TEST_I_LIMIT                       K16          * maximum number of inputs supplied by test output

  SPLC_TESTSUPPLY_LIMIT                   K10          * maximum number of test outputs

  SPLC_OEM_INT_MAX                        K16          * maximal number of arithmetical OEM configuration
          *                                              data mapped to SPLC ApiFromSafety structure

          * Possible safety states of axes groups (used for  pp_AxGrpStateReq, nn_AxGrpState, nn_AxState)
          * The numerical values are subject to change without notice!
  S_STATE_STO                             K0          * Axis/spindle stopped and shut down

  S_STATE_STO_O                           K1          * Spindle stopped and shut down (switch on without pp_AxGrpPermitDrvOn[])

  S_STATE_SOS                             K2          * Axis stopped

  S_STATE_SLS_2                           K3          * Reduced feed rate / power (SOM 2)

  S_STATE_SLS_3                           K4          * Reduced feed rate / power (SOM 3)

  S_STATE_SLS_4                           K5          * Reduced feed rate / power (SOM 4)

  S_STATE_SLI_2                           K6          * Reduced feed rate increment / power (SOM 2)

  S_STATE_SLI_3                           K7          * Reduced feed rate increment / power (SOM 3)

  S_STATE_SLI_4                           K8          * Reduced feed rate increment / power (SOM 4)

  S_STATE_SLI_S                           K9          * Reduced spindle operation increment

  S_STATE_AUTO                            K10          * Axis/spindle is active

  S_STATE_MAX                             K11          * maximum number of states

          * Possible safety states of axis groups used to identify safety operation modes (pp_GenSOM)
          * The numerical values are subject to change without notice!
  S_MODE_SOM_1                            K1          * for pp_GenSOM only: SOM 1

  S_MODE_SOM_2                            K2          * Reduced feed rate / power (SOM 2)

  S_MODE_SOM_3                            K3          * Reduced feed rate / power (SOM 3)

  S_MODE_SOM_4                            K4          * Reduced feed rate / power (SOM 4)

  S_MODE_MAX                              K5          * maximum number of modes

          * Possible stop reactions (used for pp_AxGrpStopReq, nn_AxGrpStop, nn_AxStop, nn_GenStop)
          * The numerical values are subject to change without notice!
  S_STOP_NONE                             K0          * no stop reaction active

  S_STOP_SS2                              K1          * stop on contour

  S_STOP_SS1D                             K2          * brake with maximum current and delay

  S_STOP_SS1                              K3          * brake with maximum current

  S_STOP_SS1F                             K4          * brake with maximum current because of error


*  Entity SPlcApiFromSafety describes the interface from SKERN
*  to the SPLC-program

* ================================================================
#TYPEDEF SPlcApiFromSafety
* ================================================================

  internal                                D
  NN_AxBrkReleaseReq                      M[24]               * Safety requests brake for axes (valid for 1-brake axes; for multibrake use nn_BrkReleaseReq)
  NN_AxGrpInMotion                        M[8]                * Axes in motion of axes group
  NN_AxGrpState                           D[8]                * Safety state of axes group
  NN_AxPosition                           D[24]               * Safety axes position [0,0001mm/0,0001degree]
          *                                                                           (Spindle position is in the last position)
  NN_GenSafe                              M                   * Selftest of functional safety was completed
  NN_AxSafe                               M[24]               * The axis is active, referenced and checked
  NN_BrkActivationTest                    M                   * Break activation test is active
  NN_GenOutputEnable                      M                   * output enable from SKERN to SPlc-RTS
  NN_AxState                              D[24]               * Safety state of axes
  NN_AxGrpStop                            D[8]                * Safety stop of axes group
  NN_AxStop                               D[24]               * Safety stop of axes
  NN_GenStop                              D                   * Global safety stop
  NN_MultiBrkOnAxisReleaseReq             D[24]               * Safety requests brake for individual brakes
  NN_OemInt                               D[16]               * Numeric configuration data of OEM
  NN_ActiveConfig                         D                   * Number of active configuration
*  Entity SPlcApiToSafety describes the interface from
*  the SPLC program to SKERN

* ================================================================
#TYPEDEF SPlcApiToSafety
* ================================================================

  internal                                D
  PP_AxGrpStateReq                        D[8]                * Requested safety state of axis group
  PP_AxGrpActivate                        M[8]                * Activate axis group
  PP_AxFeedEnable                         M[24]               * Permit axes movement
  PP_AxGrpStopReq                         D[8]                * Requested stop reaction
  PP_AxGrpPB                              M[8]                * State of permissive button for axis group
  PP_GenFB_NCC                            M                   * State of normally closed contact chain
  PP_GenCVO                               M                   * State of key 'control voltage on' for machine OR 'machine is on'
  PP_AxGrpPermitDrvOn                     M[8]                * State of permit axis group specific drive release / drive on
  PP_GenMKG                               M                   * At least one machine key is pressed
  PP_GenTBRK                              M                   * State of safety input test brake (TBRK)
  PP_GenSOM                               D                   * Active safety operation mode
  PP_AxFeedMax                            D[24]               * Specific limited feed [mm/min]


#TYPE
  ApiFromSafety       SPlcApiFromSafety
  ApiToSafety         SPlcApiToSafety

